  "delivered": [
    "All eight original public root-cause functions are available before mining with editable ordinary cohorts, complete Event carriers and an editable request-local shared arena. Existing replay-derived diagnostics remain available.",
    "All three RootCauseOptions members, the independent log-builder multiplier bool and custom problem_class retain native defaults and supplied-member presence. Ordered duplicate cohorts, exact source positions, seven NativeAttributeValue arms, byte strings, signed zero and semantic nonfinite values use the existing public raw-log codec.",
    "Complete four-field RootCauseRepresentation, optional eight-field RootCauseModel and seven-field tree nodes remain inspectable, including normal nullopt results and full data. Shared graph snapshots retain all nine native value fields and six context fields plus host IDs, null handles, cycles, aliases and unused arena records.",
    "Canonical before/after input, arguments and typed result artifacts preserve their actual source correspondence. Factory results, shared logs and materialized Events reopen only in compatible public operations; explicit shared-cohort reuse retains the actual arena and selected context/source positions. Arguments reopen as a real File control with complete canonical defaults.",
    "Physical multipart requests retain control/upload ownership, bytes, part order, query origin and filename presence. Native errors and optional EventLog XES exceptions remain distinct from canonical results; invalid UTF-8 category rejection follows the original algorithm.",
    "The standalone Original root-cause workspace exposes complete tables, CSV, selected records, raw responses, reports, original requests and exact artifact downloads. Completed native/API/portable/full frontend/strict build/live proofs are bound below. This native extension preserves all existing reference-package statuses; browser rendering and every strict parity gate remain open."
  ],
